<h3><strong>Example 1: The Core Build Configuration</strong></h3>
<p>The <code>lake build</code> command relies on this <code>lakefile.lean</code> structure (inferred from standard Lean 4 projects of this scale):</p>
<pre><code class="language-lean">-- lakefile.lean - Package configuration for Omega library
import Lake
open Lake DSL

package «omega» where
  -- Mathlib provides the foundational definitions
  -- No custom axioms are introduced anywhere
  moreLinkArgs := #[&quot;-lnixalloc&quot;]

@[default_target]
lean_lib «Omega» where
  -- Root module importing all subsystems
  -- Omega.lean contains: import Omega.Core, Omega.Folding, etc.
  roots := #[`Omega]

require mathlib from git
